body:
tailwind config is wrong.

There is no part in pretier-plugin-tailwindcss that modifies tailwind.config.js
(https://github.com/tailwindlabs/prettier-plugin-tailwindcss)

#### tailwind.config.js

````js
const { join } = require('path');
const prettierPlugin = require("prettier-plugin-tailwindcss");

module.exports = {
  content: [
    join(
      __dirname,
      '{src,pages,components,app}/**/*!(*.stories|*.spec).{ts,tsx,html}'
    ),
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  // "plugins": [prettierPlugin], // <- Remove this line
};
````

@ndcunningham 
You're right, you should erase both.

#### tailwind.config.js

````js
const { join } = require('path');
// const prettierPlugin = require("prettier-plugin-tailwindcss");

module.exports = {
  content: [
    join(
      __dirname,
      '{src,pages,components,app}/**/*!(*.stories|*.spec).{ts,tsx,html}'
    ),
  ],
  theme: {
    extend: {},
  },
  // "plugins": [prettierPlugin],
};
````

That's not how it's used in official documents, so there's nothing to say about the error

